  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Fix the deployed create-on-save eTag mismatch (FR-08). When a document is CREATED on save and then the
    content write follows, the create advances the item eTag — so a follow-up content write that uses the
    PRE-create precondition throws `InvalidOperationException` ("resource changed since caller last read" —
    an eTag-mismatch 500). SEQUENCE create-on-save so the content write uses the POST-CREATE eTag: create
    first, capture the fresh eTag returned by the create, then perform the content write with
    `If-Match: &lt;post-create eTag&gt;`. A genuinely concurrent EXTERNAL edit between create and content-write
    must still yield a clean 412 / ProblemDetails, NOT a 500.

    Modify the `ComposeService` save/create path. SPE writes stay behind `SpeFileStore` (ADR-007) — no
    `Microsoft.Graph` type in `Services/Compose/`. This is an ORDERED save sequence — execute the steps in
    order (`mode="prescriptive"`). Builds on the version-stamped save from 050. Every save-path change carries
    a through-the-wire seam slice (ADR-038; the seam slice is task 054).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 engineer on `ComposeService` + the SPE facade. Understands the SharePoint Embedded
    create-then-write eTag lifecycle: a create returns a fresh eTag that MUST seed the subsequent conditional
    content write, and that a stale precondition is the deployed R3 UAT failure surface.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A create-on-save sequence where the content write uses the POST-create eTag via `If-Match`, so
    create-on-save followed by a content write does NOT throw the eTag-mismatch `InvalidOperationException`;
    and a genuinely concurrent external edit still yields a clean 412 / ProblemDetails, not a 500. SPE writes
    stay behind `SpeFileStore`.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      As-built inventory (known failure surfaces from R3 UAT): "eTag mismatch after create-on-save
      (`InvalidOperationException` — resource changed since caller last read) — precondition goes stale when
      the create-on-save follow-up write advances the item eTag. → fixed by eTag sequencing (Phase 5)." Spec
      FR-08 acceptance: "create-on-save then content write does not throw the eTag mismatch." This task
      sequences the create → capture-fresh-eTag → conditional content write on the same save path 050
      version-stamps. The genuine-concurrency case (an external edit lands between create and content write)
      must still surface cleanly (412/ProblemDetails), not masked or swallowed.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs — the save/create path: sequence create-on-save so the content write uses the post-create eTag via If-Match; do not reuse the pre-create precondition</file>
      <file role="dependency">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs — create + conditional content write stay behind this facade (ADR-007); the create must return the fresh eTag for the follow-up write</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs — task 050 version-stamped save (the path this sequencing extends)</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md §5 (save + concurrency — "sequence create-on-save → fresh eTag → conditional content write")</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/spec.md FR-08</file>
      <file role="reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/as-built-inventory.md (known failure surfaces — eTag mismatch after create-on-save)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="050" status="pending">Version-stamped save path — the create-on-save sequencing extends it.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-08">Create-on-save MUST be sequenced so the content write uses the POST-create eTag (via `If-Match`); create-on-save then content write MUST NOT throw the eTag-mismatch `InvalidOperationException` (500). The content write MUST NOT reuse the pre-create precondition.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-08 negative">A genuinely concurrent EXTERNAL edit between create and content write MUST still yield a clean 412 / ProblemDetails — MUST NOT be masked into a success and MUST NOT surface as a 500.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007 / NFR-05">The create + conditional content write stay behind `SpeFileStore` — no `Microsoft.Graph` type in `Services/Compose/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">`Services/Compose/` injects NO AI internals; Tier-1 NetArchTest stays green.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">Through-the-wire seam slice required for this save-path change (authored as the task 054 seam slice). NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10 / project">State the Placement Justification (save/create orchestration stays in `Services/Compose/`; reuses `SpeFileStore` seams). Verify BFF publish size ≤60 MB compressed, report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB (incl. PDBs). No new HIGH CVE. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>SPE create-then-write eTag lifecycle; If-Match conditional write; 412 vs 500 surfacing; SPE facade; BFF hygiene</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
