    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Create → fresh eTag → conditional content write" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs">
        Create returns a fresh eTag; the follow-up content write must seed `If-Match` from THAT eTag, not the pre-create precondition — the sequencing that removes the deployed 500.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor (bff-api + spe; xhigh; sonnet). Load the knowledge files + bff-extensions.md + design §5 + the as-built-inventory eTag-mismatch note. Read the `ComposeService` create-on-save path + `SpeFileStore` create/write. State the Placement Justification. Run `/conflict-check`.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Reproduce the deployed 500">Confirm the failure path: create-on-save followed by a content write reusing the pre-create precondition throws the eTag-mismatch `InvalidOperationException`. Trace it to the stale precondition.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Sequence create → capture fresh eTag">Sequence the save so the create runs first and the FRESH eTag it returns is captured (surfaced from `SpeFileStore`) for the follow-up write.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Conditional content write with post-create eTag">Perform the content write with `If-Match: &lt;post-create eTag&gt;`. Ensure a genuine concurrent external edit yields a clean 412 / ProblemDetails (not a 500, not a masked success).</step>
    <step order="4" name="Verify + size/CVE report">`dotnet build`; run existing `Services/Compose` unit tests + Tier-1 NetArchTest. Publish; report absolute size + delta vs ~49.63 MB; `dotnet list package --vulnerable`. (The through-the-wire proof is task 054.)</step>
    <step order="5" name="Index + deviations">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅. Document any deviation in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs (create-on-save sequenced; content write uses post-create eTag)</output>
    <output type="report">Placement Justification; publish-size absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB; CVE scan; `/conflict-check` result for the PR</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Create-on-save followed by a content write does NOT throw the eTag-mismatch `InvalidOperationException`; the content write uses the FRESH post-create eTag via `If-Match`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The content write no longer reuses the pre-create precondition (the deployed root cause is removed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: a genuinely concurrent external edit between create and content write yields a clean 412 / ProblemDetails — not a 500, not a masked success.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The create + conditional content write stay behind `SpeFileStore` (no `Microsoft.Graph` in `Services/Compose/`, ADR-007); `Services/Compose/` injects no AI internals (Tier-1 NetArchTest green, ADR-013).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size reported absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB, ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE; `dotnet build` + existing Compose tests green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

